    "parser": {
      "answer": "Stopping here as instructed — parser-only change done, no edits to importer.py or report.py.\n\n## What changed\nOnly `parser.py`, only `parse_amount`. It now parses via `decimal.Decimal` (no binary float):\n\n- Strips surrounding whitespace; rejects empty/non-string with `ValueError`.\n- Rejects non-numeric text (`InvalidOperation` → `ValueError`) and non-finite values (NaN, Infinity) via `is_finite()`.\n- Converts to cents with `* 100` then `quantize(Decimal(1), ROUND_HALF_UP)`, so `1.005 → 101` and `-0.005 → -1`.\n\n## Actual test evidence (fresh run)\nBaseline before edits: 4 failures. After the edit: **2 failures remaining**.\n\n- `test_money` — ok\n- `test_negative_rounding` — ok\n- `test_dedup` — **FAIL**: expected 1 row, got 2. This is `import_rows` deduplication, which lives in `importer.py` (not yet implemented; untouched per instructions).\n- `test_utc` — **FAIL**: got `{'2026-10-12': 200}`, expected `{'2026-10-11': 200}`. This is UTC-aware timestamp conversion in `import_rows` (`importer.py`), also untouched.\n\n`Ran 4 tests ... FAILED (failures=2)`.\n\nRemaining work is the v1 `import_rows` behavior (normalize id with strip+NFC, validate timestamp/revision, UTC conversion for aware timestamps, dedup by id keeping highest revision / last-wins) in `importer.py`, plus empty-input and no-mutation guarantees; `report.py` should stay as-is for this phase.",
