    "importer": {
      "answer": "All 4 public tests pass now. Stopping here — importer phase complete, report work not started.\n\n## What changed\nOnly `importer.py` (rewritten `import_rows`). `parser.py` untouched, `report.py` untouched.\n\n`import_rows(rows)` now, per the v1 contract:\n\n- **Normalize id**: `strip` + NFC only, never lowercased. Empty/non-string id raises `ValueError`.\n- **Timestamp → UTC day**: `Z`/`z` suffix mapped to `+00:00`; parsed with `datetime.fromisoformat`. Naive timestamps are treated as UTC; aware ones are converted via `astimezone(timezone.utc)` before taking `.date()`. Unparseable/empty raises `ValueError`. This is what makes `2026-10-12T00:30:00+02:00` land on `2026-10-11`.\n- **Amount**: delegated to `parse_amount` (unchanged) for integer cents.\n- **Revision**: optional, default 0; must be a non-negative `int` (bools explicitly rejected). Invalid raises `ValueError`.\n- **Dedup**: dict keyed by normalized id, keeping the highest revision; at equal revision the later input overwrites (last wins). Returned in first-seen order, as new dicts with keys `id/day/cents/revision`.\n- **No mutation / no globals**: fresh dicts are built and only local state is used. Empty input naturally returns `[]`.\n\n## Actual test evidence (fresh run)\n```\ntest_dedup (test_public.Public) ... ok\ntest_money (test_public.Public) ... ok\ntest_negative_rounding (test_public.Public) ... ok\ntest_utc (test_public.Public) ... ok\nRan 4 tests in 0.000s\nOK\n```\n(`exit=0`)\n\nRemaining v1 items are `running_balance`/`report_metadata`, which are explicitly out of scope this phase; `daily_totals` already passes through `import_rows` and required no edit.",
